The `NL` token is dead code. Jison lex resolves rule conflicts by (1) longest match wins and (2) first-listed rule wins on ties. Since `[\s]+` (line 11) matches `
`, any input that `[
]+` could match is also matched by `[\s]+` with equal or greater length, so `[\s]+` always wins. `NL` is never produced. The grammar's `eol: NL` branch can therefore never reduce. Fix by moving the `[
]+` rule above `[\s]+` and restricting `[\s]+` to non-newline whitespace: `[ 	]+ return "SPACELIST";`.
